    "description": "Native Vulkan renderer for Minecraft 1.12.2 / Cleanroom, forked from Celeritas. Terrain, entities, items, particles, the GUI and the HUD draw through native Vulkan pipelines. With -Dceltium.vulkan.glless=true, the documented configuration, the window is created with no OpenGL context at all, the game's framebuffer is adopted into Vulkan-owned colour and depth images, and the finished frame is presented from the Vulkan swapchain; without the flag the GL bridge is used. Vanilla text draws: the font glyph path reports 52406 quads submitted, 52406 accepted, 0 refused. The vanilla post-process chains run natively only where their real input image can be supplied, and otherwise fall back to OpenGL. Still open: the entity-outline glow, FBO/post-process ownership, all-block-state and all-entity/TESR coverage, and full existing-mod compatibility. Verified on AMD RX 6400 and Intel UHD 630 only; every other vendor, driver and operating system is unverified. See docs/scope-and-limits.md section 0 for the requirement table, the measurements behind each claim and the named unverified list.",
